Various legal frameworks and principles within European human rights law work together to ensure that individuals can effectively seek redress and uphold their rights in the face of potential violations. Key among these are the provisions of the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR), particularly Articles 6, 8, and 10, which establish fundamental rights related to fair trial, privacy, and freedom of expression.

